1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Editing engaging educational tutorials from raw electronics footage

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:07,500
is incredibly time-consuming.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:11,500
Makers and students record hours of hardware builds,

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,800
but finding the right visual assets, writing kid-friendly explanations,

5
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:20,500
and sourcing matching sound effects takes hours of manual work.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Welcome to our Autonomous Agentic Tutorial Assistant,

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,500
built for the Google All Things Agentic Hackathon.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,500
The system runs fully locally, powered by the Google Agent Development Kit,

9
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:38,500
Google GenAI SDK, and Google Gemini 3.5 Flash.

10
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Our platform is an AI co-pilot that helps creators produce tutorial videos

11
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
by automatically analyzing their raw footage

12
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
and generating a complete production asset package based on their prompt.

13
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:56,000
Simply import your raw build video clips,

14
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
select a creative theme like Attack on Titan or any custom prompt,

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,500
and launch the multi-agent pipeline.

16
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
First, our Multimodal Analyzer Agent inspects the uploaded video footage.

17
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:12,500
Using Gemini 3.5 Flash multimodal vision,

18
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:16,500
it identifies the physical circuit components,

19
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:20,000
breaks down each assembly step,

20
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,000
and maps out educational analogies to make complex engineering easy for kids.

21
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:30,500
Behind the scenes, specialized agents orchestrated with the Google ADK

22
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:34,000
collaborate asynchronously to find and craft all suitable assets:

23
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:39,000
The Scriptwriter drafts a full teleprompter dialogue with synchronized timecodes.

24
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:44,500
The Dynamic Reaction Sticker Engine formulates live web queries to find real anime character frames,

25
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:49,500
transforming them into die-cut stickers for each dramatic beat.

26
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,000
And the Sound Designer synthesizes crystal-clear 44.1kHz audio cues.

27
00:01:55,500 --> 00:02:00,500
Once the agents assemble the assets, the Director Control Desk gives the creator full oversight

28
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:03,500
with a Human-in-the-Loop review loop.

29
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,000
You can request revisions or immediately approve the package for download.

30
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:13,000
Look at the generated workspace!

31
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:17,500
Every key moment is organized with custom reaction overlays,

32
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:22,000
featuring Mikasa's focused radar glare and Levi's victory poses,

33
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:26,000
complete with playable sound effects

34
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,500
and a synchronized teleprompter script tagged with inline cues.

35
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:35,500
Opening the exported folder reveals everything packaged ready for video editing:

36
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:40,000
transparent die-cut character PNG overlays,

37
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,500
broadcast WAV audio files,

38
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:47,000
structured JSON metadata,

39
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,500
teleprompter markdown,

40
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:54,500
and a standalone interactive HTML player.

41
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Please note: this entire multi-agent system runs one hundred percent locally on our machine

42
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:04,500
connecting directly to Google's official Gemini API,

43
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:09,000
as Devpost Google Cloud credits had concluded and international card issues prevented cloud billing setup.

44
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:14,000
However, the project is fully Dockerized and Cloud Run ready.

45
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:18,500
By combining the Google Agent Development Kit and Gemini 3.5 Flash,

46
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:24,000
we give creators all the assets they need to turn raw hardware footage into an unforgettable tutorial.

47
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:27,000
Thank you!
